body:

After the parity work, the owner supplied a backend and frontend product report.
Rather than accept it wholesale, the project checked each claim against the
source and wrote a triage document with prioritized tasks, evidence, proposed
approaches, and acceptance conditions. Some broad claims were narrowed, since
fresh sends already used typed-only search text, and two items were recorded as
behavior questions for the owner instead of automatic fixes.

The first three batches then landed:

- **Lifecycle and concurrency.** Per-endpoint slots became a stable gate with a
  first-in-first-out queue of cancellable waiters, retrieval warmth is committed
  only for a stored turn, and Stop during preparation is now exclusive with the
  commit. A shutdown path covers every exit. The old hand-off could not be fixed
  by moving a callback; the decision had to share the watcher's lock.
- **Privacy and correctness.** Disabled endpoints are refused, a stream must end
  with a terminator, summaries stay local to their branch even after a reroll,
  and search queries are cut at attachment headers.
- **Chat interface.** The chat view disposes cleanly on failed mounts, sending is
  gated until initialization finishes, drafts are restored only when nothing was
  stored, and an explicit Stop is separated from an aborted watch.

The race detector could not run because the environment builds without cgo, so
race-freedom rests on construction and concurrent-loop tests. A dashboard
scrolling fix followed. Many triage tasks remain open.

[Commit 78ee644](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/78ee64493668408fc6e4135cff27f4ff55e55fdd)
